The following points arose for consideration:
 1.Whether the petitioner proves that she has  been in domestic relationship with  respondents in shared household and that  she has been subjected to domestic violence Smt.Shaik Amreen vs Mr.Mushtaq Ahmed on 17 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/85515430/
7  by the respondents?
 10  Crl.Mis.51 - 2015  2. Whether the petitioner is entitled for the  reliefs as sought in the petition?
3. What order?
12. On perusal of materials placed before this Court, findings on the above points are as follows;
 Point No.1 : In the Negative;
 Point No.2 : In the Negative;
 Point No.3 : As per final order for the following;
 R EA SO NS  13.
POINT No.1: The important aspects which needs to be established in a domestic violence case are, the petitioner has to prove the domestic relationship between herself and respondent, petitioner has to show that, she resided with respondent at any point of time or lived together in shared household, petitioner has been subjected to any sort of domestic violence by the respondent during her stay in domestic relationship in a shared household.
